  "tagline": "Pioneering open-source column-store from CWI, still a lean research-grade analytical SQL database.",
  "description": "MonetDB, developed at CWI Amsterdam since the 1990s and now stewarded by the MonetDB Foundation, is one of the original column-store databases: it executes queries column-at-a-time over memory-mapped binary association tables, pioneering ideas such as database cracking and vectorized execution that later shaped DuckDB and others. It is a full SQL server with transactions, GIS, embedded Python and R UDFs and a lightweight footprint. It is a solid free analytics engine for single-server workloads and research, with a small community and limited managed or cloud options.",
